DECISION
AR-H116 is POSITIVE FOR DISCIPLINED INTEGRATION
WITH A HARD NON-UNIVERSAL ROLE-HYSTERESIS LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- multiple developmental mechanisms can compose into higher net function than a simple generalist;
- all-on adaptation produces excessive meta-overhead;
- sensing/probing/communication budgets materially improve integrated value;
- open-world model birth improves novel-regime performance;
- role persistence is not universally beneficial;
- switch friction determines whether hysteresis pays;
- integration testing changes architecture conclusions that looked universal in isolated toys.

Not demonstrated:

- real neural/runtime integration;
- spatial cell-level implementation;
- real consumer-hardware cost;
- real target-free task competence;
- interference among all historical H-series mechanisms;
- stability under months/years of accumulated structure.

NEXT HIGH-VALUE MOVE
